<node id="DISC-01">
  <data key="d0">Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">Discrepancy: Grace Period Constraint Conflict (Documentation vs Tribal Reality)</data>
  <data key="d2">PolicyValidationService</data>
  <data key="d3">1</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
  <data key="d6">provenance_validator</data>
  <data key="d7">Architecture specification claims a 30-day grace period (SME_Interview_Notes.txt:5), but operational SME notes (SME_Interview_Notes.txt:5) reveal the nightly billing batch job only enforces a 15-day cutoff, prematurely lapsing valid policies.</data>
</node>
<node id="DISC-02">
  <data key="d0">Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">Discrepancy: Pessimistic Row Locking in High-Volume Adjudication Procedure</data>
  <data key="d2">SP_PROCESS_CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d3">1</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
  <data key="d6">provenance_validator</data>
  <data key="d7">SP_PROCESS_CLAIM executes 'SELECT ... FOR UPDATE' on POLICY_MASTER rows. During claim surges, this creates blocking database locks across concurrent customer requests.</data>
</node>
<node id="DISC-03-2500">
  <data key="d0">Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">Discrepancy: Hardcoded Threshold Constant ($2500) in Source Code</data>
  <data key="d2">PolicyValidationService</data>
  <data key="d3">1</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
  <data key="d6">provenance_validator</data>
  <data key="d7">Financial threshold value $2500 is hardcoded in Java service logic instead of being configurable via enterprise rule engine.</data>
</node>
